  <prompt>
    Run the flagship graduation gate G-R3 — browser-verified on the spaarkedev1 deployment (task 081), one
    run — that proves R3's fidelity theme end-to-end. Open a formatted contract (letterhead header/footer,
    multi-level clause numbering, custom styles, a table) in Compose; edit 3 clauses incl. one bold/italic
    run change AND accept one AI redline (which must show its rationale + a grounding-tied confidence band);
    exercise the toolset — a find/replace AND a table edit in the same session; then Save and reopen and
    verify the CORE outcome: header/footer/numbering/styles/table are INTACT and the 3 edits + accepted
    redline are present as tracked changes, each anchored to the correct paragraph by `w14:paraId`. Plus the
    supporting import round-trip criterion: a doc that ALREADY has Word revisions/comments opens with them
    rendered in-editor and preserved across save. Use the `ui-test` skill (Chrome integration). This is the
    graduation gate — every G-R3 numbered step must pass in one browser run.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior QA / UAT engineer fluent in browser-based UI testing via the Spaarke `ui-test` Chrome integration,
    the Compose editor round-trip, and legal-document fidelity verification (headers/footers, multi-level
    numbering, custom styles, tables, tracked changes, paraId anchoring). Comfortable driving a full flagship
    end-to-end run and recording pass/fail per numbered criterion.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A recorded, browser-verified G-R3 pass on spaarkedev1: (1) a formatted contract renders with structure
    intact; (2) 3 clause edits (incl. a bold/italic run change) show as tracked changes and one accepted AI
    redline shows rationale + a grounding-tied confidence band; (3) find/replace + a table edit both work with
    tracked-changes marks intact; (4) after Save+reopen the header/footer/numbering/styles/table are intact and
    the 3 edits + accepted redline persist as tracked changes anchored by paraId; (5) a doc with pre-existing
    Word revisions/comments opens with them rendered and preserved across save. Each numbered G-R3 step is
    recorded pass/fail with evidence; a failure blocks graduation (does not silently pass).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      G-R3 (spec Success Criteria) is the fidelity-round-trip + toolset-demo graduation gate — the single
      flagship end-to-end that proves R3's theme (design §16 D5 / owner clarification "graduation gate =
      fidelity round-trip + toolset demo"). It runs against the full R3 deploy (task 081) on spaarkedev1, in
      the browser, one run. Steps 1–4 are the flagship list; supporting criterion 5 is the import round-trip
      (FR-24/25/26). Criteria 6–8 (publish-size/CVE, NetArchTest + slice test, real-template hardening) are
      verified elsewhere (tasks 080, 024/052, 003) and are cross-referenced, not re-run here.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="test-target">spaarkedev1 SpaarkeAi Code Page — the deployed R3 Compose editor (task 081) under browser test</file>
      <file role="skill">.claude/skills/ui-test/SKILL.md — browser-based UI testing via Chrome integration (the driver for this gate)</file>
      <file role="fixture">A formatted contract `.docx` (letterhead header/footer, multi-level clause numbering, custom styles, a table) — the flagship fixture</file>
      <file role="fixture">A `.docx` that already carries Word revisions/comments — the import round-trip fixture (supporting criterion 5)</file>
      <file role="spec">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/spec.md §Success Criteria (G-R3 flagship steps 1–4 + supporting criterion 5)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="081" status="pending">Deploy full R3 to spaarkedev1 — the known-good deployment this gate runs against.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec Success Criteria / G-R3">The gate is browser-verified on spaarkedev1, one run. Every numbered G-R3 step (1–4) + supporting criterion 5 must pass; a failure blocks graduation and is recorded, not silently passed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-07 / NFR-07 (fidelity invariant)">The core Save+reopen check MUST show header/footer/multi-level numbering/custom styles/table intact (untouched content preserved); re-serialization is cosmetic-only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-11/FR-16 / E2">Each edit + accepted redline MUST be anchored to the correct paragraph by `w14:paraId` after the round-trip.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-13/FR-14 / E3">The accepted AI redline MUST show its rationale (primary) + a grounding-tied confidence band (secondary); low-confidence edits are never auto-accepted.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-24/25/26">The import round-trip fixture MUST open with its Word revisions/comments rendered in-editor and preserved across save.</constraint>
    <constraint source="charter-6.5">A failed criterion is escalated (blocks graduation) per §6.5 — no partial/optimistic pass.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Browser-based UI testing (Chrome integration); Compose fidelity round-trip verification; paraId anchoring; E3 confidence surface</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/skills/ui-test/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/spec.md</file>
